# 1401 (fork) — project rules

AI coding is allowed in this checkout. Follow `AGENTS.md` and `DEVELOPING.md`.

## Layout

- Engine steps: `p1401/` (`scan`, `engine`/`nullmoth`, `guide`, `usbwriter`/`linuxusb`, `report`)
- Linux GTK window: `linux/1401.py` — same four steps as Windows, no second engine
- Do not edit `upstream/` (pinned copies)
- Docs for behavior: `docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md`, Linux specifics: `linux/README.md`

## Hard constraints

- No Apple code/binaries/SDK-derived files in the repo
- Third-party adds: pin URL/size/SHA-256; update `NOTICE.md` and `p1401/licenses.json`
- No secrets or personal hardware dumps
- Fail loud — never pretend a failed step succeeded
- Stick writing erases disks; prefer fake `lsblk`/ACPI fixtures in tests

## Git / gh

- Default branch: `main` tracking `fork/main` (`kik4311/1401`); do not push `origin` (`nullmoth/1401`) unless asked
- Use `gh` for PRs/issues/checks on the fork; do not PR upstream unless Lev asks
- Never commit or push AI/Cursor files (`AGENTS.md` AI rewrites, `.cursor/`) onto upstream PR branches (e.g. `linux-support`)
- Commit only when Lev asks; use `git commit -s` (DCO)
- Leave binary noise alone (e.g. accidental `macserial.exe` diffs) unless asked

## Verify

Run the smallest relevant tests from `AGENTS.md` / `DEVELOPING.md` before claiming done.
